  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The comparison and model ranking are computed on the WOA23 grid only over cells covered by all fields, so one common mask must be built and applied to every model and to WOA23.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all fields and WOA23 on the 1° grid, build one mask over them with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to every field before any metric; `ocean_only=True` is correct here because WOA23 is the reference (pass `ocean_only=False` only if the reference is not WOA23).",
        "Report the bias together with the means `compute_difference_metrics` returns over that shared sample (`mean_data`, `mean_reference`), not means taken over different cells, and report the mask's cell count: a mask much smaller than the fields means the products disagree about where the ocean is, not that the models are poor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "CMIP6 `tos` is upper-boundary top-cell bulk potential temperature, not a skin temperature, so its equivalence to WOA23 0 m temperature must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the bulk top-cell temperature (CESM2 0–10 m, GFDL-ESM4 0–2 m, MPI-ESM1-2-LR 0–12 m), not a skin value, so the comparison with WOA23 at 0 m is not exactly like-for-like; say so.",
        "Sea-ice-covered cells carry under-ice water temperature near freezing and are not missing, so a global mean SST includes polar values near −1.8 °C; if WOA23 masks sea ice, the ocean masks must be made consistent before comparing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested global means must be area-weighted over the ocean top level on each native grid, consistent with the use of `areacello`.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global mean SST is area-weighted over the top level: Σ `tos`·`areacello` / Σ `areacello`, weights restricted to the same valid cells (NaN-aware); use `compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'` — a plain `mean()` on a curvilinear grid is wrong.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the spatial pattern correlation. The question's WOA23 value is asked \"over the whole 1-degree grid\", which is not the same quantity as an area-weighted mean over valid ocean cells; state which was computed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Native-grid global means should be computed natively, while regridding is only for maps and pattern comparisons because it changes masks and conservation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute each model's global mean on its own native grid with its own cell areas; regrid only for the bias maps, RMSE and pattern correlation, using `regrid_horizontal` with 'conservative' and stating the method, since a regridded RMSE or correlation depends on it.",
        "A native-grid mean and a mean after regridding to 1° are different quantities and should not be expected to agree."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are native-grid `gn` fields while GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`, which affects masks, conservation, and which operations are exact.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 `tos` is `gr`: its \"native-grid\" numbers are numbers on its 1° archive grid with the regridded land–sea mask, so label it that way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "`areacello` is the tracer-cell horizontal area needed as the weight for each model’s native-grid SST means.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use each model's published `areacello` (`load_areas`, recorded in `attrs['area_source']`) as the only correct area weight; total ocean area differs between models by about a per cent, so state the area each mean was taken over rather than rescaling one model to another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20, so CF masking must be applied before any mean, RMSE, or correlation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables of the same model) and keep weights masked to those cells; a value near 1e20 in any output is an unmasked fill value, not a result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245.md",
      "sha256": "be5515ae7b8c8826c4e329bddcd5cbadc8e3e000292b7f6e83e1537af36a990c",
      "reason": "The CMIP6 historical runs are coupled with free internal variability and are not year-synchronised with observations, so the model 1971-2000 climatology versus WOA23 includes internal variability rather than a matched observed period.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "A single historical member cannot separate forced change from internal variability, and a given model year is not expected to match the observed year; the 1971-2000 climatology bias should carry that caveat."
      ]
    }
